# Everything at once: titles and formulas that write themselves in and
# turn into the next step (docs/38, 39), titles with their own times, labels
# (always on, timed, and formulas), orbits, a moon, a fly-by past a moving
# planet (docs/32), a planned hit that sticks (docs/18), easing, fades,
# see-through glass, arrows, a graph that draws itself (docs/42) and a shape
# that morphs (docs/43). No coordinates anywhere: the solver places it all.
# ./main scenes/showcase.dan --aa

scene "showcase"
title "A solar system, solved" write 1.5s
title "a probe flies past the moving planet" 4s-12s
title "a comet hits it, and sticks" 13s-20s
math "F = G\frac{m_1 m_2}{r^2}" 1s-24s write 2s becomes "F = \frac{GMm}{r^2}" at 6s-7s becomes "v = \sqrt{\frac{GM}{r}}" at 12s-13s

sun    = sphere big gold important label math "M" always
rock   = icosahedron grey near sun label "a rock" 0s-6s
glass  = cube teal in_front_of sun fades_in 1s-3s fades_out 20s-23s
planet = octahedron red orbits sun 1 turn 0s-24s label math "m" always
moon   = tetrahedron tiny white orbits planet 3 turns 0s-24s label "moon" 2s-10s
probe  = cube small blue flies_past planet 4s-12s smooth label "probe" 4s-12s
comet  = pyramid small white fades_in 9s-11s label "comet" 9s-20s
wave   = graph "sin(x)" from -6.28 to 6.28 small teal below sun create 2s-5s
badge  = square yellow filled small left_of sun create 1s-2s becomes circle at 8s-9s becomes star at 16s-17s
comet hits planet at 16s from 12s sticks

arrow sun planet gold
arrow comet planet teal 12s-16s
